<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ajax the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Telamonian Ajax</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ajax the Great is a hero of Greek mythology, son of Telamon king of Salamis, who fights in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a> as the mightiest Greek warrior after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achilles">Achilles</a>. After losing the contest for Achilles' armour to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odysseus">Odysseus</a> he took his own life, a story told in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophocles">Sophocles</a>' tragedy Ajax. His half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teucer">Teucer</a> was said to have founded Salamis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ajax-the-great.jpg" alt="Ajax the Great" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antimenes Painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antimenes_Painter_-_Black-figure_Amphora_with_Ajax_Carrying_the_Dead_Achilles_-_Walters_4817_-_Side_A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
